payoff-markers = Dots mark commissioning and break-even. Click a plant name above to hide or show its curve.
payoff-horizon = Chart shows { $years } years; the table includes longer payoffs. Recovery includes construction time.
payoff-plant = Plant
payoff-revenue = Revenue / month
payoff-fuel = Fuel / month
payoff-upkeep = Upkeep / month
payoff-net = Net income / month
payoff-recovery = Recovery from order
payoff-years = { $years } years
payoff-never = Never
payoff-assumptions = Idealized full utilization: all output is sold at today's price, with fixed costs and average months from a 365-day year. Construction is paid in monthly instalments, with no income until commissioning. Excludes financing, start-ups, grid connections, regulatory charges, depreciation and replacement costs; curves can extend beyond a plant's book life.
payoff-renewables = Generators run at full nameplate output 24 hours a day. Solar, wind and hydro ignore daylight, weather and water limits, so their actual payoff will be longer.
payoff-geothermal = Geothermal assumes successful exploration and a full-strength field without decline or makeup drilling. Exploration payments precede the remaining construction payments.
build-ccgt-loss-warning = At the current price of { $price }, this plant loses money even at full output: about { $loss } per month after fuel and upkeep.
